Z||000020||BENGAL4||02-08-2000||09:44 AM||||Eric & Chadman - I lived in Licking county for over a year back in 1990. I ran the bowling center in Utica. I love driving the back roads out there. You just have to watch out for Barney Fife in St Louisville. 6 cops in a town of 300 people. What a speed trap. Another speed trap is New Albany. The funeral director from Utica got pulled over in his hearse there. He was on his way to Columbus to pick up. His excuse was he had Led Zeppelin to loud on his stereo and he wasn't paying attention.  They ticketed him anyway. 28 in a 25mph zone. Rough.||||reg||6
Z||000021||Scott2M4||02-08-2000||11:56 AM||||BOY!  You guys aren't gonna let me live down that Fox & Hound thing, are ya!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I get the three major car mags (MT, R&T, C&D) and at least one of them always mentions doing some of their road tests somewhere in Southern Ohio.  Any idea where?  Wouldn't it be cool if we took our babies out there (wherever it is) and caught them testing the new MR2 roadster.  I bet we'd be mentioned in the article!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I plan to have mine washed for this trip.  I was embarrassed when Bill's beautiful, clean GT had to park next to my salt-ball at Cracker Barrel.  And mine was the only one to get commented on about being dirty!  Go figure!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><B>fiero56</B> - If you're worried about the mileage on the Formula, you're more than welcome to ride with me.  Just don't talk to me about stereos while I'm driving, OK!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>OK, so far we have:<P>Scott2M4<BR>ChadMan<BR>william_thorniii (maybe)<BR>BENGAL4<BR>fiero56 (maybe)<BR>Eric<BR>BOILERMAKER (probably)<BR>Formula (probably - weather?)<P>Anyone else?||||reg||1
Z||000022||william_thorniii||02-08-2000||12:05 PM||||Scott,<P>It wasn't the dirt that I commented on... it was the fact that you had parked it under the sprinkler that night.  For the record, I washed mine the day before... but then made a 250 mi round trip that night.  <P>LOL re: "Just don't talk to me about stereos while I'm driving, OK!?"<P>Never ever drive with a wild animal in the car either... right Monkey?<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>||||reg||10
Z||000023||fiero56||02-08-2000||12:20 PM||||WIlliam, you were worried. I thought I was going to be pulling the front end of an '85GT out of the back of my car.<P>I admit, mine was the dirtiest there. Black paint, white salt, UGLY. Scott just had these little frozen water dropplets everywhere. <P>Scott, I get those same mags and always wonder where in Ohio they talk about going. It's not the mileage on my car I worry about(150K right now), I drove that same stretch of road every week while going to school in Columbus, and it is very boring to drive alone. I thought you were heading North after the Fiero trip?||||reg||1
Z||000024||william_thorniii||02-08-2000||12:41 PM||||Drew,<P>I was never worried about actually making contact.  I knew that I had plenty of room to stop and also another lane to work with.  I was and am embarrassed that I didn't see you all stopping though.  Too much stimulation is involved with trying to point out indian mounds associated with stereo tips and tricks and group vehicle navigation.  I never expected a stop once we got the the park... Oh well, live and learn!<P>Sorry,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
