Z||000033||Scott2M4||02-15-2000||04:57 PM||||Just making sure we've not forgotten about this ...<P>I've got directions to the Hickory House for those of us coming from the south:<P><B>-</B> Get to the interchange of I-270 and Route 315 on Columbus' north side.  It's best to stay out of the city and use the 270 bypass because Columbus is experiencing heavy road construction.<BR><B>-</B> At the 270/315 interchange, take 315 North for about 3 miles to Powell Road.<BR><B>-</B> Turn left on Powell Road.  Drive about 2 miles - you'll reach the village of Powell.<BR><B>-</B> Turn right on Liberty.  Hickory House is about 1/4 mile up Liberty in a strip mall on the right.  The address is 240 N. Liberty Road.<P><B>BOILERMAKER</B> - Not sure where exactly you're coming from but, once in Ohio, it's a straight shot across I-70 to I-270.<P>So, Saturday, 2/26, 12:00 at the Hickory House in Columbus.  After we eat, gab, eat more, gab more ..., it's off to shop for Fieros with <B>ChadMan</B>!  Just kidding, Chad.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Can you imagine the expression on a seller's face when 10 Fieros pulled up to look at their car!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Actually, I believe we're planning a little cruise down 315 along the river.  Someone please correct me if I'm wrong.<P>If I've missed anything, please let me know.  Also, let me know if you're still planning to attend so I know whether or not we need to send out search parties when you don't show up.<P>Other than that, see everyone on 2/26!||||reg||1
Z||000034||william_thorniii||02-15-2000||05:57 PM||||Scott,<P>Still not sure if I can talk the fiancee into it. I am presently trying to work out a deal that if we get to do Fiero activities by day that perhaps we will go shopping/dancing at night.  That would be the ULTIMATE compromise for us since they are our most loved/hated things respectively... I know what you are all wondering... "Hmmmmmm, I wonder which one likes the shopping and dancing and which one likes Fiero's"  Just to clear it up, that woman is a Fiero-nut.  LOL.  I will try to work on her again tonight.  If that doesn't work maybe we can get a mass spam campaign going on?  LOL I hate having to indicate when I am joking to avoid flames.  It's kind of like a comic that laughs at his/her own jokes.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||12
