Z||000070||87ECO5||02-27-2000||02:23 PM||||Just got back from Mansfield.  MAN!, what a weekend!  Beautiful weather, great friends, lots of Fieros and a few Miller Genuine Drafts!  Tell me, does it get any better than that!?<P><B>ChadMan</B>, <B>Eric</B>, <B>Stormy</B> and <B>2M4 Dale</B> - it was an absolute pleasure to meet the four of you!  <B>BENGAL4</B> - it was great to see you again!  I'm sorry we didn't get to do the cruise but I had a blast anyway!  I love you guys ... but you're not getting my Bud Light!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'll post a few photos from the trip as soon as I get them developed.<P>For those asking about the next outing, check out the <B>'Ohio Fieros Icebreaker Cookout'</B> thread.||||reg||6
Z||000071||87ECO5||02-27-2000||04:58 PM||||That's right.  I was <B>Scott2M4</B>, then I was <B>The Fierohaulic Formerly Known As Scott2M4</B>, then I'll just be <B>The Fierohaulic</B>, finally, I'll simply be known by the Pegasus symbol!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000072||BENGAL4||02-27-2000||08:16 PM||||Nice meeting you Chad and Eric. Always a pleasure to see you Scott. My wife enjoyed meeting you guys also. She used to think our community was a little wierd, but you guys changed her mind. She has also met Boilermaker and Monkeyman. They couldn't change her mind, because she said they are just as obsessed with Fieros as I am. I guess as she meets more members, she will mellow out on the whole Fiero thing. She even wants to go to the cookout.||||reg||1
