Z||000074||87ECO5||03-19-2000||12:33 AM||||FINALLY managed to get those pictures developed from the trip (sorry about the poor picture quality)!  Here we go ...<P>This first photo is of the cars and their owners.  From left to right - <B>BENGAL4</B> (and his wife, Stormy, behind him, <B>Eric</B> and <B>ChadMan</B>:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_gang1.jpg">  <P>Another view of the cars:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_gang2.jpg">  <P>The participants (clockwise from top left - <B>BENGAL4</B>'s 1986 GT, <B>87ECO5</B>'s 1987 economy coupe, <B>ChadMan</B>'s 1988 sport coupe and <B>Eric</B>'s 1987(?) GT):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_participants.jpg">  <P>Finally, a photo of the awesome auxiliary gauges in <B>Eric</B>'s GT:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_dials.jpg">  <P>I had a TON of fun, guys!  We'll have to do it again sometime soon!  Oh wait, we are on 4/1!  Silly me!<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 03-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000075||ChadMan||03-19-2000||10:30 AM||||Hey Scott, thanks for posting these pix!  Those are four nice Fieros if you ask me - though I could be biased.<P>I've got my wife about 1/2 convinced that coming to the picnic 4/1 is a good idea.  We'll see how the move goes next week...||||reg||10
